Code and invented-data checks only. No historical account, financial run, actual execution claim or financial GO has been created. The separately sealed five-year source preparation and independent source audit passed; that success grants no financial authority.

The fixed cohort is original STATIC50_OLD_NO_REEXPANSION LOW/MID/HIGH then CORE VOL_MANAGED_HOLD LOW/MID/HIGH, each one 10,000-USDT wallet over [2021-04-02,2026-01-01), all1,735days seen DEV. This controller admits only the first predeclared STATIC LOW resource pilot. It counts once if complete; the other five require a fresh root release after resource verification. No profitable-year/tier selection, annual closes/reset/reseed, retry, snapshot resume or parameter change exists.

- continuous_admission: exact new root/review/source-audit/code/array/calendar/cohort/resource binding, permanent claim and live capability. Old annual and generated capabilities confer no authority.
- continuous_inputs and the separately late-imported continuous_provider: finance-bound recapture using unchanged pure parsers/2022 memory-only normalization under the unchanged clean financial-graph guard; exact prepared feature/event/quality/endpoint identity; eight immutable saved arrays, no target regeneration. Provider consumes57 selected month slices once. It is imported only after guard exit.
- native_adapter: exact annual actual initialization field seam plus inherited D finance/type bindings, single simulator/provider/wallet, original typed2022 and separate2024 quality OR predicate, lifetime risk state, one global terminal signal end‚àí61minutes with60 later genuine opens.
- continuous_output: original durable daily chunk/annual-marker path, truthful actual header, gzip exact roundtrip, physical temporary-byte/log budgets, no duplicate whole-minute export.
- run_continuous: stdlib-only pre-numerical bootstrap, inherited nonblocking own/shared CPU45 leases, immutable claim before spawn, PID/start-tick and asynchronous parent-death binding, one owned worker, resource caps, bounded observations, sticky pause. Worker writes a revoked candidate; supervisor-observed EXIT0 and saved verification precede terminal publication.
- continuous_terminal: externally bound identity/process/schema, pre-allocation daily NPZ headers, full/prefix calendar and annual-state/chunk bits, unchanged native40 reconstruction/account contract, distinct paid/conditional/residual/native-halt/operational outcomes. Original roundoff-sensitive diagnostic stays untouched.

Accepted future bounds:2,400 combined CPU seconds,2,700 wall seconds,4.5GB RSS stop,7GB AS hard cap,700MB case including log,4.2GB cohort,1.5GB free-disk floor. Prelaunch lower(host,cgroup-visible remaining) available memory must be at least5.5GB; missing cgroup visibility is reported as uncertainty. Stricter aggregate RSS and transient-write accounting do not raise those bounds. Every cap failure preserves outputs/claim and pauses. A zero-written-row unexpected native halt has no new chunk format: its tiny halt witness is preserved separately from an export interruption, never relabeled or replayed.

Generated checks run in separate fresh processes, using the supported coin_partial_restore_20261014/.venv/bin/python -B and assigned CPU: native6tests; admission/input8tests (invented1735-day array/source tables, no native full-horizon run); runner15temporary-process tests; terminal2tests (real4-day invented native candidate, observed childEXIT0, real saved validator, tamper/header negatives). Independent review is separate and must bind the final manifest before any root financial GO.

Read-boundary disclosure: while inspecting the frozen terminal clock, an outside-guard recursive read-only grep scanned the already-authorized original2021 DEV source-preparation tree. Its raw-container read extent is unverified; no binary data was decoded and no wallet/provider or financial run resulted. It is not part of any clean source-guard evidence. Old source attempts, failure audit, successful preparation and independent audit remain unchanged.
