This additive v2 preserves immutable v1, its independent review and failed actual source attempt001. Attempt001 stopped with observed shell exit1 after 41.597 CPU seconds because the unchanged CORE builder's full canonical proof path lazily loaded H090 source code inside the strict source guard. No account or provider was constructed and no prepared payload was accepted.

The only target integration change is explicit core._h090() code-only preloading before the unchanged whole-invocation source guard, alongside the existing original/quality/codec preload. CORE computes H090 provenance internally while producing selected HOLD targets; this adds no strategy or target. The vendor/account loader is not preloaded. A new checkpoint records that boundary. Failure receipts now directly record source-scope/body-phase revocation. The end-to-end invented capture test resets the exact H090 cache to None immediately before the real entry, reproducing the cold actual invocation while keeping all data invented.

All other code and the complete source catalog are byte-identical to v1. The original v1 README describes the unchanged gate, parsers, five-year union, all six target/covariance/complete-provenance parity, literal funding and composed 2022/2024 quality qualifications. The source code still admits no finance/account/provider/claims/download/holdout/publication action. V2 requires a newly matching independent review and fresh exact SOURCE-only GO. Root delegated one same-scope source-only retry after that review passes; financial execution still needs separate authorization.

Use the supported coin_partial_restore_20261014/.venv/bin/python -B. The root-authorized CPU0 source wrapper calls the reviewed prepare_source_only API under external affinity and the existing source bounds (900 CPU seconds,1800 wall seconds,3GB AS,1GiB output,1.5GB disk floor). The CLI's generated/review affinity choices remain7/8; the API does not change authority or guard checks. Preserve every failure artifact and observed tool exit.
